      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(plugins): bound safeHashFile in installed-plugin-index-hash with size cap",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`safeHashFile` in `src/plugins/installed-plugin-index-hash.ts:30` reads the entire file synchronously into memory with no size limit before hashing — despite being named \"safe\". Plugin install records can reference arbitrarily large files (binaries, model files, bundled assets). A multi-GB `readFileSync` will crash the Node process before the `catch` block can run, since `readFileSync` is synchronous and OOM happens inline.\n\nThe sister function `safeFileSignature` (line 49) already uses `statSync` to get file metadata, showing the pattern exists — but `safeHashFile` never checks file size.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nA function named \"safe\" should not have unbounded sync reads. The `catch` block can handle ENOENT and permission errors, but cannot prevent OOM from multi-GB files.\n\n## What Changed\n\nAdded a `statSync` pre-check before the `readFileSync`:\n1. Checks file existence\n2. Rejects non-regular files\n3. Rejects files exceeding 50 MiB cap\n4. Only reads files that pass the checks\n\n## Evidence\n\n**All 27 plugin index tests pass:**\n\n```\n✓ src/plugins/installed-plugin-index.test.ts (27 tests)\n```\n\n50 MiB is well above any legitimate plugin install file (plugin manifests are < 1 MiB, bundled assets are typically < 20 MiB).",
        "branch": "fix/bound-plugin-index-hash",
